Data licence - moved, this file is a pointer only.

This file used to say "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)" over library/dataset/, kb/ and
docs/FINDINGS.md. That was wrong in the direction that mattered: CC BY permits commercial reuse, so the
curated layer - our translations, our voice index, our adjudication and gap notes - was licensed to the
world for resale on the day the repo went public, while README.md described the same material as the thing
we intend to sell.

Read the outbound terms in:

    LICENSING.md        the three layers, and the machine-readable scope block the build enforces
    LICENSE_DATA.md     the precise terms for the curated layer (CC BY-NC 4.0 + commercial licence)
    LICENSE_POLICY.md   what may enter the dataset at all (bucket A/B/C) - stricter, and unchanged

The two obligations the old file imposed are still imposed, now in LICENSE_DATA.md: preserve per-passage
provenance (work + locator) in anything you redistribute, and do not add living-tradition material without
the consent of the lineage that holds it.
